  "title": "Sharp connection-Dirac spectral-sum domination for graph complexes",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every nonempty finite abstract simplicial complex G whose faces all have cardinality at most two, let L_G be the unweighted face-intersection matrix and D_G the unaugmented oriented-incidence Dirac matrix defined in problem.md. For every integer 1 <= k <= |G|, S_k(L_G) >= S_k(D_G) + 1, where S_k sums the k largest eigenvalues with multiplicity. The constant 1 is sharp, already at k=1 for the complex consisting of one edge and its two vertices. Disconnected complexes, isolated vertices, and non-bipartite graphs are included. This is only the dimension-at-most-one case; the original arbitrary-dimensional comparison remains unresolved.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
